node.doctext:
Do yourself a favour (additionally to care for proper indentation) and use <b>descriptive</b> variable names;
<code>
$price = $hashref->{price};
$title = $hashref->{title};
</code>
instead of 
<c>
$tempdesc = $hashref->{price};
$tempdesc2 = $hashref->{title};
</c>
Saves you a lot of looking up, wondering and bug hunting.

<div class="pmsig"><div class="pmsig-241598">
<br><br><b>holli</b><br><br>
<i>You can lead your users to water, but alas, you cannot drown them.</i>
</div></div>
